  m_Name: Level 2 Questions
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::HokkienQuizQuestionBank
  questions:
  - question: "What is the origin of Hsinchu Pork Ball (\u65B0\u7AF9\u8089\u4E38)\uFF1F"
    choices:
    - Created by a son for his blind mother
    - Created by fisherman to make pork easier to store
    - Created by workers to make pork easier to carry
    - Created by a mother for her young son
    choiceExplanations:
    - "Hsinchu Pork Ball (\u65B0\u7AF9\u8089\u4E38) is a meat ball made from beating
      pork into a paste and shaping into balls. It is a dish said to have been created
      during the Ming dynasty by a devoted son for his blind mother, to help her
      eat pork more easily. It originated from Fujian (which is part of Minnan) and
      was brought to Taiwan during the Qing dynasty. Hsinchu is the most famous producer
      of pork balls in Taiwan."
    - This is made up.
    - This is made up.
    - This is made up.
    correctAnswerIndex: 0
  - question: Which of the following is equivalent to 30% off?
    choices:
    - "\u6253\u4E09\u6298 "
    - "\u6253\u56DB\u6298"
    - "\u6253\u4E03\u6298 "
    - "\u6253\u4E09\u5341\u6298"
    choiceExplanations:
    - "The phrase \u201C\u6253X\u6298\u201D is equivalent to \u201C100%-10X% off\u201D"
    - "The phrase \u201C\u6253X\u6298\u201D is equivalent to \u201C100%-10X% off\u201D"
    - "The phrase \u201C\u6253X\u6298\u201D is equivalent to \u201C100%-10X% off\u201D"
    - "The phrase \u201C\u6253X\u6298\u201D is equivalent to \u201C100%-10X% off\u201D"
    correctAnswerIndex: 0
  - question: If you ask for a discount, which of the following responses from the
      vendor is NOT a rejection?
    choices:
    - "\u4ECA\u5929\u6CA1\u6709\u6298\u6263\u3002"
    - "\u5468\u672B\u624D\u6709\u6D3B\u52A8\u3002"
    - "\u6211\u5011\u5DF2\u7D93\u662F\u9019\u908A\u6700\u4FBF\u5B9C\u7684\u4E86\u3002"
    - "\u7ED9\u4F60\u6253\u516B\u6298 "
    choiceExplanations:
    - "This means \u201Cthere is no discount today\u201D, which is a rejection."
    - "This means \u201Cthere\u2019s only discounts on weekends\u201D, which is a
      rejection."
    - "This means \u201COurs is already the cheapest here\u201D, which is a rejection."
    - The vendor offered a 20% off discount!
    correctAnswerIndex: 3
